European Balancing Market Forecasting & Risk Intelligence Platform
Overview

The European Balancing Market Forecasting & Risk Intelligence Platform is an end-to-end energy analytics project designed to analyze electricity balancing markets across major European countries.

## 🌐 Live Demo

The interactive Streamlit dashboard is available here:

👉 https://industry-projects-5mshb3elzypw7kr7ajwtdm.streamlit.app


The platform combines:

Data engineering pipelines
Electricity market analytics
Forecasting models
Renewable generation analysis
Imbalance risk assessment
Interactive dashboard visualization

The objective is to simulate a real-world energy analytics workflow supporting market analysts, trading teams, and risk management functions.

Business Problem

Electricity balancing markets play a critical role in maintaining grid stability by correcting deviations between electricity demand and generation.

Increasing renewable penetration introduces additional uncertainty due to:

Weather dependency
Generation volatility
Forecast errors
Price fluctuations
Imbalance exposure

Energy market participants require analytical tools to:

Forecast system conditions
Monitor imbalance risk
Quantify market stress
Identify operational risks

This project develops a complete analytics platform addressing these challenges.

Market Coverage

The platform analyzes five European electricity markets:

Country	Market Area
Germany	DE-LU
France	FR
Italy	IT
Netherlands	NL
Spain	ES

Analysis period:

2020 - 2026

